Step 1: Check OpenSSL Installation [openssl version ]
Step 2: Generate Private Key  [openssl genrsa -out private_key.pem 2048]
Step 3: Display Private Key Details [openssl rsa -in private_key.pem -text -noout]
Step 4: Generate Public Key from Private Key  [openssl rsa -in private_key.pem -pubout -out public_key.pem]
Step 5: View Public Key [openssl rsa -pubin -in public_key.pem -text -noout]
Program (Shell Script Version) 
[#!/bin/bash 
 echo "Generating RSA Private Key..." 
 openssl genrsa -out private_key.pem 2048 
 echo "Generating Public Key..." 
 openssl rsa -in private_key.pem -pubout -out 
 public_key.pem 
 echo "Keys Generated Successfully!" 
 echo "Private Key File: private_key.pem" 
 echo "Public Key File: public_key.pem"]
Save the file as: [generate_keys.sh]
Give execution permission: [chmod +x generate_keys.sh]
Run: [./generate_keys.sh]
Verification 
Check private key: [cat private_key.pem]
Check public key: [cat public_key.pem] 
